<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/harness/report/batch',
        '/harness/report/ratio',
        '/harness/measure/measure',
        '/harness/report/emulated-dom',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/harness/tests/measure.test.ts',
            from: ["test('time() throws while the counters are armed'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/harness/tests/measure.test.ts',
            from: ["test('time() under bun refuses on the emulated DOM'"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Time two rankings of the deals in one batch">
        <p>Hand <code>time</code> every arm at once. It interleaves them, grows the batch until a
            sample clears the clock, and runs the first arm again as its own control.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="shared" code={`
            import { time } from '@abide/harness/measure'

            const batched = time({
                case: 'top five deals',
                arms: {
                    sort: () => [...deals].sort(byAmount).slice(0, 5),
                    toSorted: () => deals.toSorted(byAmount).slice(0, 5),
                },
            })
            batched.samples.toSorted.nanoseconds // per op, the minimum over reps
            batched.floor // the A/A spread a ratio has to clear
        `} />
        <p>Run it under <code>bun run bench</code> or a serial test. A parallel worker
            throws.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Count and time an op in separate passes">
        <p>The counters run inside the path they count, so <code>time</code> throws while a
            <code>measure</code> case is open. Hand the counts in as <code>work</code>
            instead.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="shared" code={`
            import { measure, time } from '@abide/harness/measure'

            measure(() => time({ case: 'nested', arms: { one: () => {} } }))
            // throws: counting and timing are mutually exclusive passes
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Refuse a duration from an emulated DOM">
        <p>Under bun with a DOM preloaded, <code>time</code> throws. Time a DOM op in a browser,
            where the lane runs too.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="shared" code={`
            import { time } from '@abide/harness/measure'

            time({ case: 'render', arms: { one: () => {} } })
            // throws: happy-dom can produce a count, not a millisecond
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
